"\n\n\n\n\n## Review\nA story of a generation on the brink of extinction due to a lethal toxic nano-dust called .  \nA common subject in SF is indeed the extinction of mankind.  \nIf the production is possible, it seems like a material and fun element that could be made into a movie.  \n\nThe duality of mankind in dealing with the resistant species that always appears in such stories is also revealed in this book.  \nAre they beings that must be sacrificed for the sake of mankind and the public interest?"